  "question_stem": "In a certain chemical process a substance $A$ reacts with and reduces a substance $B$. The masses of $A$ and $B$ at time $t$ after the start of the process are $x$ and $y$ respectively. It is given that $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t} = -0.2xy$ and $x = \\frac{10}{(1+t)^2}$. At the beginning of the process $y = 100$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t} = -\\dfrac{2y}{(1 + t)^2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\ln y = \\dfrac{2}{1 + t} - 2 + \\ln 100, \\quad \\text{or } y = 100e^{\\frac{2}{1 + t} - 2}$$"
  ],
